     6	## 3.7 — essential supremum at zero measure (fidelity hold)
     7	
     8	The printed third-edition pp.65–66 define the threshold set using **all real
     9	α**, even for nonnegative functions. With the zero measure on a singleton
    10	and the zero function, every real threshold belongs to the set. The note
    11	after 1.18 explicitly permits the zero measure as a positive measure. It is
    12	unbounded below, so the stated real infimum does not exist; an extended-real
    13	interpretation gives minus infinity rather than a nonnegative norm.
