   218	Source: the [1987 third-edition scan and OCR](https://djvu.online/file/NKmAEzkLVs8Io), printed pp. 61–71. The [publisher's contents](https://www.mheducation.co.in/real-and-complex-analysis-9789355326119-india) independently confirms Chapter 3 and its title. Numbered headings 3.1–3.17 are verified; no invented numbering. OCR loses inequality bars: endpoint-sensitive statements below were checked against the scan. Exercises are excluded.
   219	
   220	**Count:** 17 numbered items: 10 theorems, 5 definitions, 2 numbered remarks. All 17 are inventoried; no original numbered item is yet counted proved. The counterexample and repair for 3.7 are separate results, not completion of that item.
   221	
   222	Mathlib was inspected at `d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612`. `U` = already in Mathlib in usable form; `V` = variant requiring a faithful restatement/bridge; `M` = missing packaged result after the searches described below. This classifies reuse, not book-node completion. For definitions, it classifies the corresponding representation.
   223	
   224	| Node | Kind; printed page | Subject | Claim | Exact Mathlib route / remaining issue |
   225	|---|---|---|---|---|
   226	| 3.1 | Definition; 61 | Interval convexity | V | `ConvexOn`; associated slope and derivative characterizations require separate restatements. |
   227	| 3.2 | Theorem; 61–62 | Convexity implies continuity | U | `ConvexOn.continuousOn` on an open interval, `Analysis/Convex/Continuous.lean`. |
   228	| 3.3 | Theorem; 62–63 | Jensen inequality | V | `ConvexOn.map_integral_le`, `Analysis/Convex/Integral.lean`, assumes a closed convex set and integrability of the composition. Rudin permits an open interval and an infinite upper integral; those cases must be retained. |
   229	| 3.4 | Definition; 63 | Conjugate exponents | V | `Real.HolderConjugate` and `ENNReal.HolderConjugate`; bridge finite parameters and the endpoint pair. |
   230	| 3.5 | Theorem; 63–65 | Hölder and Minkowski | U | `MeasureTheory.lintegral_mul_le_Lp_mul_Lq`, `MeasureTheory.lintegral_Lp_add_le`, `MeasureTheory/Integral/MeanInequalities.lean`; finite exponents, nonnegative extended-valued measurable functions. |
   231	| 3.6 | Definition; 65 | Finite-exponent Lp norm | V | `MeasureTheory.eLpNorm`, `MeasureTheory.MemLp`; distinguish actual measurable representatives from AE strong measurability. |
   232	| 3.7 | Definition; 65–66 | Essential supremum; L∞ | V; FIDELITY HOLD | `MeasureTheory.essSup`, `eLpNorm_exponent_top`. The printed real-threshold set is unbounded below for zero measure; see the event below. |
   233	| 3.8 | Theorem; 66 | Product in L1; Hölder including endpoints | V | `MeasureTheory.MemLp.mul`, `MeasureTheory.eLpNorm_smul_le_mul_eLpNorm`, `LpSeminorm/CompareExp.lean`. The printed L∞ convention must first be repaired explicitly. |
   234	| 3.9 | Theorem; 66 | Lp addition; triangle inequality | V | `MeasureTheory.MemLp.add`, `MeasureTheory.eLpNorm_add_le`, `LpSeminorm/TriangleInequality.lean`; endpoint depends on 3.7. |
   235	| 3.10 | Remarks; 66–67 | Vector space; AE quotient metric | V | `MeasureTheory.Lp.instNormedAddCommGroup`, `Lp.instModule`, `MemLp.toLp_eq_toLp_iff`, `Lp.dist_def`; separate representative/quotient bridge. |
   236	| 3.11 | Theorem; 67–68 | Lp completeness, including infinity | V | `MeasureTheory.Lp.instCompleteSpace`, `LpSpace/Complete.lean`; direct after the explicit convention decision for 3.7. |
   237	| 3.12 | Theorem; 68 | AE convergent subsequence | U | `MeasureTheory.tendstoInMeasure_of_tendsto_eLpNorm` then `TendstoInMeasure.exists_seq_tendsto_ae`, `Function/ConvergenceInMeasure.lean`. |
   238	| 3.13 | Theorem; 69 | Simple-function density | V | `MeasureTheory.Lp.simpleFunc.isDenseEmbedding`, `Function/SimpleFuncDenseLp.lean`; translate its subtype to finite-range measurable functions with finite-measure support. |
   239	| 3.14 | Theorem; 69 | Compactly supported continuous density | V | `MeasureTheory.MemLp.exists_hasCompactSupport_eLpNorm_sub_le`, `Function/ContinuousMapDense.lean`; Mathlib assumes `μ.Regular`, whereas Rudin uses the completion/regularity package of 2.14. Preserve that distinction. |
   240	| 3.15 | Remarks; 69–70 | Euclidean Lp completions | V | Combine 3.11/3.14 with `BoundedContinuousFunction.toLp_injective` and positive-open-set Lebesgue measure; includes the different infinity completion. |
   241	| 3.16 | Definition; 70 | Continuous functions vanishing at infinity | U | `ZeroAtInftyContinuousMap`, `Topology/ContinuousMap/ZeroAtInfty.lean`. |
   242	| 3.17 | Theorem; 70–71 | C₀ completion of Cc | M (assembled theorem) | `ZeroAtInftyContinuousMap.instCompleteSpace` supplies completeness. No packaged Cc-to-C₀ density/completion theorem found in `Topology/ContinuousMap`, `Analysis`, or whole-tree density searches. Urysohn cutoff construction remains. |
   243	
   244	The 17 classifications are U=4, V=12, M=1. These are source-level claims checks, not successful Lean invocations of every listed route.
   245	
   246	## Fidelity event 3.7
   247	
   248	The [p.65 scan](https://djvu.online/jpg/N/K/m/NKmAEzkLVs8Io/077.webp) specifies real thresholds, with no nonnegativity restriction. On a singleton with zero measure and zero function every real threshold qualifies. The note after 1.18 (p.16) explicitly permits the identically zero measure. Thus that set has no real lower bound and no real infimum in the order-theoretic sense. Using an extended-real infimum instead gives minus infinity, which is not a nonnegative norm. This is a defect in the definition's zero-measure case, not a claimed failure of the standard Lp theorems.
   249	
   250	`Chapter03.lean` stops the printed definition, proves the unboundedness counterexample, and proves an explicitly labelled correction using thresholds in `ℝ≥0∞`. The corrected essential supremum is zero for zero measure, is an almost-everywhere upper bound, and is the least such bound. No downstream node is counted complete by silently adopting this repair. Coordinator disposition is recorded in `QUEUE.md`.
     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Build a source snapshot with fresh project outputs and pinned dependency cache.
     3	
     4	The live checkout and its outputs are preserved. The temporary snapshot is
     5	retained for inspection. No git operation or dependency installer is invoked.
     6	"""
     7	
     8	from __future__ import annotations
     9	
    10	import hashlib
    11	import json
    12	import os
    13	from pathlib import Path
    14	import shutil
    15	import subprocess
    16	import sys
    17	import tempfile
    18	
    19	
    20	PIN = "d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612"
    21	TOOLCHAIN = "leanprover/lean4:v4.34.1"
    22	
    23	
    24	def inputs(book: Path) -> dict[str, bytes]:
    25	    names = {"lakefile.toml", "lake-manifest.json", "lean-toolchain"}
    26	    for directory, children, files in os.walk(book):
    27	        children[:] = [name for name in children if name != ".lake"]
    28	        for name in files:
    29	            if name.endswith(".lean"):
    30	                names.add(str((Path(directory) / name).relative_to(book)))
    31	    return {name: (book / name).read_bytes() for name in sorted(names)}
    32	
    33	
    34	def main() -> int:
    35	    book = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
    36	    snapshot = inputs(book)
    37	    manifest = json.loads(snapshot["lake-manifest.json"])
    38	    mathlib = next(p for p in manifest["packages"] if p["name"] == "mathlib")
    39	    if mathlib["rev"] != PIN or snapshot["lean-toolchain"].decode().strip() != TOOLCHAIN:
    40	        raise RuntimeError("required Lean/Mathlib pins changed")
    41	    lake = shutil.which("lake")
    42	    if lake is None:
    43	        raise RuntimeError("lake is not provisioned; this script does not install it")
    44	    packages = (book / ".lake" / "packages").resolve(strict=True)
    45	    revision = subprocess.check_output(
    46	        ["git", "-C", str(packages / "mathlib"), "rev-parse", "HEAD"], text=True
    47	    ).strip()
    48	    if revision != PIN:
    49	        raise RuntimeError("dependency checkout does not match the Mathlib pin")
    50	    if not (packages / "mathlib/.lake/build/lib/lean/Mathlib.olean").is_file():
    51	        raise RuntimeError("dependency cache absent; first run lake exe cache get")
    52	
    53	    fresh = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="rca-a-clean-build-"))
    54	    for name, content in snapshot.items():
    55	        destination = fresh / name
    56	        destination.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    57	        destination.write_bytes(content)
    58	    (fresh / ".lake").mkdir()
    59	    (fresh / ".lake/packages").symlink_to(packages, target_is_directory=True)
    60	    hashes = {name: hashlib.sha256(content).hexdigest() for name, content in snapshot.items()}
    61	    (fresh / "input-sha256.json").write_text(json.dumps(hashes, indent=2) + "\n")
    62	    print(f"Snapshot: {fresh}", flush=True)
    63	    print("Fresh project output directory: absent before build", flush=True)
    64	    print(f"Command: {lake} build (cwd={fresh})", flush=True)
    65	    print(f"Dependency revision: {revision}", flush=True)
    66	    print("Input SHA256: " + json.dumps(hashes, sort_keys=True), flush=True)
    67	    result = subprocess.run([lake, "build"], cwd=fresh, check=False)
    68	    print(f"Build exit code: {result.returncode}", flush=True)
    69	    if inputs(book) != snapshot:
    70	        raise RuntimeError("live build inputs changed during validation; snapshot is no longer current")
    71	    print("Live inputs still match the validated snapshot; snapshot retained.", flush=True)
    72	    return result.returncode
    73	
    74	
    75	if __name__ == "__main__":
    76	    try:
    77	        sys.exit(main())
    78	    except (OSError, RuntimeError, ValueError, StopIteration, subprocess.CalledProcessError) as exc:
    79	        print(f"FAIL: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
    80	        sys.exit(1)
